Z||000000||fierosound||11-28-1999||07:42 PM||||Anyone know what code signifies a 3.4L V6 in the VIN#?  I've found the codes for 2.8, 3.1, 3.4 DOHC, 3.8 etc., but I am still looking for 3.4 codes, both RWD and FWD.  Also, is there anything to differentiate between iron block/iron heads and iron block/alum heads engines?<P>One last thing...  if the engine is already out, what code should I be looking for on the block that identifies it as a 3.4L?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 11-28-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tim||11-29-1999||11:08 AM||||The 3.4 block has external ribs on the size of the block, 2.8 and 3.1 have not.  2.8 and 3.1 has the liter size cast on the side of the block.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierosound||11-29-1999||11:24 AM||||What I've got so far:<P>S = 2.8 V6<BR>W = 2.8 V6<BR>9 = 2.8 V6 (Fiero ONLY)<BR>M = 3.1 V6<BR>T = 3.1 V6 Turbocharged<BR>V = 3.1 V6 Turbocharged<BR>X = 3.4 DOHC V6<P>What about 3.4 iron block/iron heads from Camaros and APVs?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 11-29-1999).]||||reg||10
